IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc-core-persons`
IMPORT `uc4-sch8-sch9-treated`

-- Tests of uc4-sch8-sch9-treated.l4: Schedules 8 and 9 and regulations 39(6), 39(7), 40(5), 40(6).
-- Expected values are written by hand from the text, beside the assertion.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Builders for the facts records (there is no record update, so every fixture is built whole).
GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN, b IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A BOOLEAN, d IS A BOOLEAN, e IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Sch 8 para 1 treatment facts`
`test — para 1` a b c d e MEANS `Sch 8 para 1 treatment facts` WITH
    `receiving regular weekly treatment by way of haemodialysis for chronic renal failure` IS a
    `receiving treatment by way of plasmapheresis` IS b
    `receiving regular weekly treatment by way of total parenteral nutrition for gross impairment of enteric function` IS c
    `recovering from any of those forms of treatment` IS d
    `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the claimant should be treated as having limited capability for work` IS e

`test — a doctor` MEANS Practitioner WITH
    `registered medical practitioner` IS TRUE
    `registered nurse` IS FALSE
    `occupational therapist or physiotherapist` IS FALSE
    `registered with a regulatory body established under section 60 of the Health Act 1999` IS FALSE

`test — nobody who is a health care professional` MEANS Practitioner WITH
    `registered medical practitioner` IS FALSE
    `registered nurse` IS FALSE
    `occupational therapist or physiotherapist` IS FALSE
    `registered with a regulatory body established under section 60 of the Health Act 1999` IS FALSE

GIVEN patient IS A BOOLEAN, rehab IS A BOOLEAN, advised IS A BOOLEAN, adviser IS A Practitioner, recovering IS A BOOLEAN, satisfied IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Sch 8 para 2 hospital facts`
`test — para 2` patient rehab advised adviser recovering satisfied MEANS `Sch 8 para 2 hospital facts` WITH
    `undergoing medical or other treatment as a patient in a hospital or similar institution` IS patient
    `attending a residential programme of rehabilitation for the treatment of drug or alcohol dependency` IS rehab
    `has been advised to stay for a period of 24 hours or longer following medical or other treatment` IS advised
    adviser IS adviser
    `recovering from such treatment` IS recovering
    `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the claimant should be treated as having limited capability for work` IS satisfied

GIVEN nation IS A `Nation of Great Britain`, excluded IS A BOOLEAN, prevented IS A BOOLEAN, suspected IS A BOOLEAN, s45a IS A BOOLEAN, tb IS A BOOLEAN, scotdisease IS A BOOLEAN, scotcontam IS A BOOLEAN, compensation IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Sch 8 para 3 facts`
`test — para 3` nation excluded prevented suspected s45a tb scotdisease scotcontam compensation MEANS `Sch 8 para 3 facts` WITH
    `nation in which the claimant is` IS nation
    `excluded or abstains from work pursuant to a request or notice in writing lawfully made or given under an enactment` IS excluded
    `otherwise prevented from working pursuant to an enactment` IS prevented
    `it is known or reasonably suspected that the claimant is infected or contaminated, or has been in contact with a case` IS suspected
    `incidence or spread of infection or contamination within section 45A(3) of the Public Health (Control of Disease) Act 1984 for which regulations are made under Part 2A of that Act` IS s45a
    `tuberculosis or an infectious disease to which regulation 9 of the Public Health (Aircraft) Regulations 1979 or regulation 10 of the Public Health (Ships) Regulations 1979 applies` IS tb
    `infectious disease within section 1(5) of the Public Health etc (Scotland) Act 2008, or exposure to an organism causing that disease` IS scotdisease
    `contamination within section 1(5) of that Act, or exposure to a contaminant` IS scotcontam
    `sections 56 to 58 of the Public Health etc (Scotland) Act 2008 (compensation) apply to it` IS compensation

GIVEN ill IS A BOOLEAN, risk IS A BOOLEAN, adjustments IS A BOOLEAN, medication IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Sch 8 para 4 risk facts`
`test — para 4` ill risk adjustments medication MEANS `Sch 8 para 4 risk facts` WITH
    `suffering from a specific illness, disease or disablement` IS ill
    `by reason of it there would be a substantial risk to the physical or mental health of any person were the claimant found not to have limited capability for work` IS risk
    `the risk could be reduced by a significant amount by reasonable adjustments being made in the claimant's workplace` IS adjustments
    `the risk could be reduced by a significant amount by the claimant taking medication prescribed by a registered medical practitioner treating the claimant` IS medication

GIVEN lifethreatening IS A BOOLEAN, uncontrollable IS A BOOLEAN, uncontrolled IS A BOOLEAN, cause IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Sch 8 para 5 disease facts`
`test — para 5` lifethreatening uncontrollable uncontrolled cause MEANS `Sch 8 para 5 disease facts` WITH
    `suffering from a life threatening disease` IS lifethreatening
    `there is medical evidence that the disease is uncontrollable by a recognised therapeutic procedure` IS uncontrollable
    `there is medical evidence that the disease is uncontrolled by a recognised therapeutic procedure` IS uncontrolled
    `there is a reasonable cause for the disease not to be controlled by a recognised therapeutic procedure` IS cause

GIVEN age IS A BOOLEAN, benefits IS A LIST OF Benefit
GIVETH A `Sch 8 para 6 facts`
`test — para 6` age benefits MEANS `Sch 8 para 6 facts` WITH
    `reached the qualifying age for state pension credit` IS age
    `entitled to` IS benefits

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Sch 8 para 1. (a) haemodialysis, (b) plasmapheresis, (c) total parenteral nutrition; or recovering where the Secretary of State is satisfied.
#ASSERT `Sch 8 para 1 — receiving certain treatments` (`test — para 1` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Sch 8 para 1 — receiving certain treatments` (`test — para 1` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Sch 8 para 1 — receiving certain treatments` (`test — para 1` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Sch 8 para 1 — receiving certain treatments` (`test — para 1` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- Recovering without the Secretary of State's satisfaction is not enough; satisfaction alone is not enough.
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 8 para 1 — receiving certain treatments` (`test — para 1` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 8 para 1 — receiving certain treatments` (`test — para 1` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 8 para 1 — receiving certain treatments` (`test — para 1` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))

-- Sch 8 para 2. In hospital: undergoing treatment as a patient (advised by a health care professional to stay 24 hours or longer), or recovering with the Secretary of State satisfied; or on a residential rehabilitation programme.
#ASSERT `Sch 8 para 2 — in hospital` (`test — para 2` TRUE FALSE TRUE `test — a doctor` FALSE FALSE)
-- Not advised to stay 24 hours or longer: not regarded as undergoing treatment as a patient (sub-paragraph (3)).
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 8 para 2 — in hospital` (`test — para 2` TRUE FALSE FALSE `test — a doctor` FALSE FALSE))
-- Advised, but not by a health care professional: the same.
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 8 para 2 — in hospital` (`test — para 2` TRUE FALSE TRUE `test — nobody who is a health care professional` FALSE FALSE))
-- A residential rehabilitation programme for drug or alcohol dependency is included (sub-paragraph (2)), read as not subject to (3): fork F-sch8-2.
#ASSERT `Sch 8 para 2 — in hospital` (`test — para 2` FALSE TRUE FALSE `test — nobody who is a health care professional` FALSE FALSE)
-- Recovering, with the Secretary of State satisfied.
#ASSERT `Sch 8 para 2 — in hospital` (`test — para 2` FALSE FALSE FALSE `test — a doctor` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 8 para 2 — in hospital` (`test — para 2` FALSE FALSE FALSE `test — a doctor` TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 8 para 2 — in hospital` (`test — para 2` FALSE FALSE FALSE `test — a doctor` FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT `Sch 8 para 2(2) and (3) — the claimant is regarded as undergoing treatment as a patient in a hospital or similar institution` (`test — para 2` TRUE FALSE TRUE `test — a doctor` FALSE FALSE)

-- Sch 8 para 3. England and Wales: infection within s 45A(3) of the 1984 Act, or tuberculosis etc.
#ASSERT `Sch 8 para 3 — prevented from working by law` (`test — para 3` England TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Sch 8 para 3 — prevented from working by law` (`test — para 3` Wales FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Scotland: the Scottish limbs only count there, and need sections 56 to 58 (compensation) to apply.
#ASSERT `Sch 8 para 3 — prevented from working by law` (`test — para 3` Scotland TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Sch 8 para 3 — prevented from working by law` (`test — para 3` Scotland TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 8 para 3 — prevented from working by law` (`test — para 3` Scotland TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
-- An English infection limb does not help a claimant in Scotland, and a Scottish limb does not help one in England.
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 8 para 3 — prevented from working by law` (`test — para 3` Scotland TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 8 para 3 — prevented from working by law` (`test — para 3` England TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE))
-- Excluded or prevented is needed; so is the known or suspected infection.
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 8 para 3 — prevented from working by law` (`test — para 3` England FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 8 para 3 — prevented from working by law` (`test — para 3` England TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))

-- Sch 8 para 4. Risk to self or others, unless the risk could be reduced by workplace adjustments or by medication.
#ASSERT `Sch 8 para 4 — risk to self or others` (`test — para 4` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 8 para 4 — risk to self or others` (`test — para 4` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 8 para 4 — risk to self or others` (`test — para 4` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 8 para 4 — risk to self or others` (`test — para 4` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 8 para 4 — risk to self or others` (`test — para 4` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE))

-- Sch 8 para 5. Life threatening disease: uncontrollable or uncontrolled (medical evidence); if uncontrolled, a reasonable cause.
#ASSERT `Sch 8 para 5 — life threatening disease` (`test — para 5` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Sch 8 para 5 — life threatening disease` (`test — para 5` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 8 para 5 — life threatening disease` (`test — para 5` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 8 para 5 — life threatening disease` (`test — para 5` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 8 para 5 — life threatening disease` (`test — para 5` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE))

-- Sch 8 para 6. The qualifying age for state pension credit and entitlement to DLA, Scottish adult DLA, PIP or ADP.
#ASSERT `Sch 8 para 6 — disabled and over the age for state pension credit` (`test — para 6` TRUE (LIST `personal independence payment`))
#ASSERT `Sch 8 para 6 — disabled and over the age for state pension credit` (`test — para 6` TRUE (LIST `disability living allowance`))
#ASSERT `Sch 8 para 6 — disabled and over the age for state pension credit` (`test — para 6` TRUE (LIST `Scottish adult disability living allowance`))
#ASSERT `Sch 8 para 6 — disabled and over the age for state pension credit` (`test — para 6` TRUE (LIST `adult disability payment`))
-- Attendance allowance is not on the Schedule 8 list (it is on Schedule 9's).
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 8 para 6 — disabled and over the age for state pension credit` (`test — para 6` TRUE (LIST `attendance allowance`)))
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 8 para 6 — disabled and over the age for state pension credit` (`test — para 6` FALSE (LIST `personal independence payment`)))
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 8 para 6 — disabled and over the age for state pension credit` (`test — para 6` TRUE EMPTY))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Regulation 39(6) and (7): any circumstance in Schedule 8; paragraphs 4 and 5 only where the claimant does not have limited capability for work as determined by an assessment under Part 5.
`test — nothing in Schedule 8` MEANS `Sch 8 circumstances` WITH
    `paragraph 1 facts` IS `test — para 1` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
    `paragraph 2 facts` IS `test — para 2` FALSE FALSE FALSE `test — a doctor` FALSE FALSE
    `paragraph 3 facts` IS `test — para 3` England FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
    `paragraph 4 facts` IS `test — para 4` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
    `paragraph 5 facts` IS `test — para 5` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
    `paragraph 6 facts` IS `test — para 6` FALSE EMPTY

`test — Schedule 8 paragraph 1 only` MEANS `Sch 8 circumstances` WITH
    `paragraph 1 facts` IS `test — para 1` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
    `paragraph 2 facts` IS `test — para 2` FALSE FALSE FALSE `test — a doctor` FALSE FALSE
    `paragraph 3 facts` IS `test — para 3` England FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
    `paragraph 4 facts` IS `test — para 4` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
    `paragraph 5 facts` IS `test — para 5` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
    `paragraph 6 facts` IS `test — para 6` FALSE EMPTY

`test — Schedule 8 paragraph 4 only` MEANS `Sch 8 circumstances` WITH
    `paragraph 1 facts` IS `test — para 1` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
    `paragraph 2 facts` IS `test — para 2` FALSE FALSE FALSE `test — a doctor` FALSE FALSE
    `paragraph 3 facts` IS `test — para 3` England FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
    `paragraph 4 facts` IS `test — para 4` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
    `paragraph 5 facts` IS `test — para 5` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
    `paragraph 6 facts` IS `test — para 6` FALSE EMPTY

`test — Schedule 8 paragraph 5 only` MEANS `Sch 8 circumstances` WITH
    `paragraph 1 facts` IS `test — para 1` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
    `paragraph 2 facts` IS `test — para 2` FALSE FALSE FALSE `test — a doctor` FALSE FALSE
    `paragraph 3 facts` IS `test — para 3` England FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
    `paragraph 4 facts` IS `test — para 4` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
    `paragraph 5 facts` IS `test — para 5` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
    `paragraph 6 facts` IS `test — para 6` FALSE EMPTY

#ASSERT NOT (`reg 39(6) and (7) — the claimant is to be treated as having limited capability for work` `test — nothing in Schedule 8` FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 39(6) and (7) — the claimant is to be treated as having limited capability for work` `test — Schedule 8 paragraph 1 only` FALSE
-- Paragraph 1 is not subject to paragraph (7): it counts even when an assessment has found limited capability for work.
#ASSERT `reg 39(6) and (7) — the claimant is to be treated as having limited capability for work` `test — Schedule 8 paragraph 1 only` TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 39(6) and (7) — the claimant is to be treated as having limited capability for work` `test — Schedule 8 paragraph 4 only` FALSE
-- Paragraph 4 does not apply where limited capability for work is determined by an assessment under this Part.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 39(6) and (7) — the claimant is to be treated as having limited capability for work` `test — Schedule 8 paragraph 4 only` TRUE)
#ASSERT `reg 39(6) and (7) — the claimant is to be treated as having limited capability for work` `test — Schedule 8 paragraph 5 only` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 39(6) and (7) — the claimant is to be treated as having limited capability for work` `test — Schedule 8 paragraph 5 only` TRUE)

-- =========================================================================================================
-- Schedule 9.
GIVEN progressive IS A BOOLEAN, months IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN Illness
`test — illness` progressive months MEANS Illness WITH
    `suffering from a progressive disease` IS progressive
    `months within which death in consequence of that disease can reasonably be expected` IS months

GIVEN pregnant IS A BOOLEAN, seriousrisk IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Sch 9 para 2 pregnancy facts`
`test — Sch 9 para 2` pregnant seriousrisk MEANS `Sch 9 para 2 pregnancy facts` WITH
    `a pregnant woman` IS pregnant
    `there is a serious risk of damage to her health or to the health of her unborn child if she does not refrain from work and work-related activity` IS seriousrisk

GIVEN receiving IS A BOOLEAN, likely IS A BOOLEAN, recovering IS A BOOLEAN, satisfied IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Sch 9 para 3 cancer treatment facts`
`test — Sch 9 para 3` receiving likely recovering satisfied MEANS `Sch 9 para 3 cancer treatment facts` WITH
    `receiving treatment for cancer by way of chemotherapy or radiotherapy` IS receiving
    `likely to receive such treatment within 6 months after the date of the determination of capability for work and work-related activity` IS likely
    `recovering from such treatment` IS recovering
    `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the claimant should be treated as having limited capability for work and work-related activity` IS satisfied

GIVEN ill IS A BOOLEAN, risk IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Sch 9 para 4 risk facts`
`test — Sch 9 para 4` ill risk MEANS `Sch 9 para 4 risk facts` WITH
    `suffering from a specific illness, disease or disablement` IS ill
    `by reason of it there would be a substantial risk to the physical or mental health of any person were the claimant found not to have limited capability for work and work-related activity` IS risk

GIVEN age IS A BOOLEAN
      benefits IS A LIST OF Benefit
      dla IS A BOOLEAN
      sadla IS A BOOLEAN
      pip IS A BOOLEAN
      adp IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Sch 9 para 5 facts`
`test — Sch 9 para 5` age benefits dla sadla pip adp MEANS `Sch 9 para 5 facts` WITH
    `reached the qualifying age for state pension credit` IS age
    `entitled to` IS benefits
    `entitled to the care component of disability living allowance at the highest rate` IS dla
    `entitled to the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest rate in accordance with regulation 6(4) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025` IS sadla
    `entitled to the daily living component of personal independence payment at the enhanced rate` IS pip
    `entitled to the daily living component of adult disability payment at the enhanced rate in accordance with regulation 5(3) of the Disability Assistance for Working Age People (Scotland) Regulations 2022` IS adp

-- Sch 9 para 1: terminally ill (the core's definition: a progressive disease and death expected within 12 months).
#ASSERT `Sch 9 para 1 — terminal illness` (`test — illness` TRUE 12)
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 9 para 1 — terminal illness` (`test — illness` TRUE 13))
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 9 para 1 — terminal illness` (`test — illness` FALSE 6))

-- Sch 9 para 2: a pregnant woman and a serious risk of damage to her health or her unborn child's.
#ASSERT `Sch 9 para 2 — pregnancy` (`test — Sch 9 para 2` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 9 para 2 — pregnancy` (`test — Sch 9 para 2` TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 9 para 2 — pregnancy` (`test — Sch 9 para 2` FALSE TRUE))

-- Sch 9 para 3: chemotherapy or radiotherapy now, likely within 6 months, or recovering; and the Secretary of State is satisfied.
#ASSERT `Sch 9 para 3 — receiving treatment for cancer` (`test — Sch 9 para 3` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Sch 9 para 3 — receiving treatment for cancer` (`test — Sch 9 para 3` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Sch 9 para 3 — receiving treatment for cancer` (`test — Sch 9 para 3` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- The satisfaction qualifies all three limbs (fork F-sch9-1): receiving treatment is not enough without it.
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 9 para 3 — receiving treatment for cancer` (`test — Sch 9 para 3` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 9 para 3 — receiving treatment for cancer` (`test — Sch 9 para 3` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE))

-- Sch 9 para 4: a substantial risk to the health of any person were the claimant found not to have limited capability for work and work-related activity.
#ASSERT `Sch 9 para 4 — risk to self or others` (`test — Sch 9 para 4` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 9 para 4 — risk to self or others` (`test — Sch 9 para 4` TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 9 para 4 — risk to self or others` (`test — Sch 9 para 4` FALSE TRUE))

-- Sch 9 para 5: the qualifying age and attendance allowance, pension age disability payment, or one of four component-and-rate conditions.
#ASSERT `Sch 9 para 5 — disabled and over the age for state pension credit` (`test — Sch 9 para 5` TRUE (LIST `attendance allowance`) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Sch 9 para 5 — disabled and over the age for state pension credit` (`test — Sch 9 para 5` TRUE (LIST `pension age disability payment`) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Sch 9 para 5 — disabled and over the age for state pension credit` (`test — Sch 9 para 5` TRUE EMPTY TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Sch 9 para 5 — disabled and over the age for state pension credit` (`test — Sch 9 para 5` TRUE EMPTY FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Sch 9 para 5 — disabled and over the age for state pension credit` (`test — Sch 9 para 5` TRUE EMPTY FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Sch 9 para 5 — disabled and over the age for state pension credit` (`test — Sch 9 para 5` TRUE EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- Being entitled to disability living allowance is not enough: the care component at the highest rate is what the paragraph names.
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 9 para 5 — disabled and over the age for state pension credit` (`test — Sch 9 para 5` TRUE (LIST `disability living allowance`) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`Sch 9 para 5 — disabled and over the age for state pension credit` (`test — Sch 9 para 5` FALSE (LIST `attendance allowance`) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE))

-- Regulation 40(5) and (6).
`test — Schedule 9, nothing applies` MEANS `Sch 9 circumstances` WITH
    `paragraph 1 facts` IS `test — illness` FALSE 0
    `paragraph 2 facts` IS `test — Sch 9 para 2` FALSE FALSE
    `paragraph 3 facts` IS `test — Sch 9 para 3` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
    `paragraph 4 facts` IS `test — Sch 9 para 4` FALSE FALSE
    `paragraph 5 facts` IS `test — Sch 9 para 5` FALSE EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

`test — Schedule 9, terminal illness only` MEANS `Sch 9 circumstances` WITH
    `paragraph 1 facts` IS `test — illness` TRUE 3
    `paragraph 2 facts` IS `test — Sch 9 para 2` FALSE FALSE
    `paragraph 3 facts` IS `test — Sch 9 para 3` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
    `paragraph 4 facts` IS `test — Sch 9 para 4` FALSE FALSE
    `paragraph 5 facts` IS `test — Sch 9 para 5` FALSE EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

`test — Schedule 9, paragraph 4 only` MEANS `Sch 9 circumstances` WITH
    `paragraph 1 facts` IS `test — illness` FALSE 0
    `paragraph 2 facts` IS `test — Sch 9 para 2` FALSE FALSE
    `paragraph 3 facts` IS `test — Sch 9 para 3` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
    `paragraph 4 facts` IS `test — Sch 9 para 4` TRUE TRUE
    `paragraph 5 facts` IS `test — Sch 9 para 5` FALSE EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

#ASSERT NOT (`reg 40(5) and (6) — the claimant is to be treated as having limited capability for work and work-related activity` `test — Schedule 9, nothing applies` FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 40(5) and (6) — the claimant is to be treated as having limited capability for work and work-related activity` `test — Schedule 9, terminal illness only` FALSE
-- Paragraph 1 is not subject to paragraph (6).
#ASSERT `reg 40(5) and (6) — the claimant is to be treated as having limited capability for work and work-related activity` `test — Schedule 9, terminal illness only` TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 40(5) and (6) — the claimant is to be treated as having limited capability for work and work-related activity` `test — Schedule 9, paragraph 4 only` FALSE
-- Paragraph 4 does not apply where limited capability for work and work-related activity is determined by an assessment under this Part.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 40(5) and (6) — the claimant is to be treated as having limited capability for work and work-related activity` `test — Schedule 9, paragraph 4 only` TRUE)
